# UI/UX

Applies to **every** user: Super Admin, church staff, attendance officers, and any later member/visitor flows. Follow ISO 9241-110: self-descriptive, consistent, error-tolerant, suited to the task.

## Task flow

- One primary action per page. Secondary actions are quieter.
- Destructive actions need a confirm.
- After save: toast or inline success, then stay in context or return to the list — never a blank screen.
- Auth: clear next step after login (platform vs church). Failed login says so without leaking whether the email exists, if that is the security choice.
- Filters, search, and pagination: preserve list state in the URL when bookmarking helps.

## States (every list, form, and auth page)

Ship **loading**, **empty**, **error**, and **populated**. Empty copy must say what to do, not “No data”. Login and forgot-password need error and pending states too.

## Forms (TanStack Form or auth forms)

- Visible labels. Required fields marked. Inline field errors, not only a banner.
- Disable double-submit. Show pending on the submit button.
- Unsaved-change warning on edit pages.

## Consistency

- Same object = same layout everywhere it appears.
- Platform shell, church shell, and auth share type, color, radius, and components. Different nav/layout, not a different product.
- Do not invent a new table, modal, or button style per feature.

## Copy

- Sentence case. Domain words: church, member, zone, service — not “workspace” or “persona”.
- Errors say how to fix, in the user’s language (staff vs later member portal).
